# Rank 1565 / CVE-2024-32970: Phlex's javascript:-URL guard normalized
# href values by stripping only tabs, spaces and newlines, so a scheme
# carrying other control characters bypassed the check and executed
# script through the rendered attribute (XSS, CWE-79; fixed alongside
# the XSS browser-test suite). The attribute writer in lib/phlex/
# sgml.rb did `next if lower_name == "href" && v.to_s.downcase.tr(
# "\t \n", "").start_with?("javascript:")` -- browsers strip the full
# control-character set when parsing URLs, so "jav\x01ascript:" or
# scheme spellings with embedded controls survive the tr and reach
# the href values. The fixing commit
# (confirmed, its lib/phlex/sgml.rb hunk is the security change,
# bundled with 6613 lines of XSS fixtures and browser tests): the
# normalization becomes `v.to_s.downcase.tr("^a-z:", "").start_with?(
# "javascript:")` -- only lowercase letters and the colon survive, so
# no control character can hide inside the scheme -- and the unsafe
# attribute-name check normalizes with tr("^a-z-", ""). No pool
# correction.
#
# ATTENTION, guard-normalization strength. The check exists and runs
# -- its defect is that the character class it strips is weaker than
# the parser it defends against, the same present-but-incomplete
# family as ranks 1551 (first-quote-only escaping), 1522
# (bracket-blind host checks) and 1564 (unquoted bind types): nothing
# can ask "does this scheme normalization remove everything the
# downstream URL parser ignores", which requires knowing both
# vocabularies. A binding on Phlex's own href writer would detect
# this library rather than the weakness. Measured on the real code:
# scanning lib/ reports the same 3 findings at both revisions
# (VYQL-INJ-004 heuristics on phlex/kit.rb's const_added -- nothing
# on sgml.rb's attribute path). No ENGINE-GAPS.md entry: the piece is
# normalization-strength vocabulary, not a localised construct. No
# definition change shipped. Spec cve_rank1565 records the weak tr
# form and the strict normalization, both asserting reject
# VYQL-INJ-004: when normalization-strength vocabulary lands, the
# weak-tr form must flip to expect.

test "rank1565: the href scheme check strips three characters only"
  lang ruby
  file lib/phlex/sgml.rb
  reject VYQL-INJ-004
  code
  ```
  module Phlex
    module SGML
      def unsafe_write_attributes(attributes)
        attributes.each do |k, v|
          if k == :href
            lower_name = "href"
            next if lower_name == "href" && v.to_s.downcase.tr("\t \n", "").start_with?("javascript:")
          end

          if HTML::EVENT_ATTRIBUTES.include?(k.to_s.downcase) || k.to_s.match?(/[<>&"']/)
            raise ArgumentError, "Unsafe attribute name detected: #{k}."
          end

          yield %( #{k}="#{v}")
        end
      end
    end
  end
  ```

test "rank1565: the fixed revision keeps only letters and the colon"
  lang ruby
  file lib/phlex/sgml.rb
  reject VYQL-INJ-004
  code
  ```
  module Phlex
    module SGML
      def unsafe_write_attributes(attributes)
        attributes.each do |k, v|
          if k == :href
            lower_name = "href"
            next if lower_name == "href" && v.to_s.downcase.tr("^a-z:", "").start_with?("javascript:")
          end

          if HTML::EVENT_ATTRIBUTES.include?(k.to_s.downcase.tr("^a-z-", "")) || k.to_s.match?(/[<>&"']/)
            raise ArgumentError, "Unsafe attribute name detected: #{k}."
          end

          yield %( #{k}="#{v}")
        end
      end
    end
  end
  ```
